      "message": "I think this whole solution could be reduced to a few lines by making use of Spring Kafka topic check and Spring RetryTemplate. Basically I am proposing that we just keeping trying to start the listeners until they stop throwing exceptions. Something like this:\n\n    @Component\n    @RequiredArgsConstructor\n    public class KafkaStartup {\n        private final KafkaListenerEndpointRegistry registry;\n\n        @Async\n        @EventListener(ApplicationReadyEvent.class)\n        public void startListenersWhenReady() {\n            var retry \u003d new RetryTemplate(RetryPolicy.builder().backOff(new FixedBackOff()).build());\n            retry.invoke(() -\u003e registry.getListenerContainers().stream()\n                    .filter(container -\u003e !container.isRunning())\n                    .forEach(MessageListenerContainer::start));\n        }\n    }\nTo enable topic validation, just change application.yaml:\n\n    spring:\n      kafka:\n        listener:\n          missing-topics-fatal: ${TOPIC_VALIDATION:false}\n\n\nNote there are other variants like `ExponentialBackOff`; custom logging can be added with `RetryListener`, though I would guess spring kafka would already log failures.",
